{"name":"Phellodendron Amurense","hex":"#f3c13a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Phellodendron amurense","blocks":[{"text":"Phellodendron amurense is a species of tree in the family Rutaceae, commonly called the Amur cork tree. It is a major source of huáng bò, one of the 50 fundamental herbs used in traditional Chinese medicine. The Ainu people used its fruit, called \"shikerebe-ni\", as a painkiller. It is known as hwangbyeok in Korean and (キハダ) kihada in Japanese."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Phellodendron_amurense_Morton.jpg/330px-Phellodendron_amurense_Morton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phellodendron_amurense","wikidata":"Q481711"},{"title":"Phellodendron","blocks":[{"text":"Phellodendron, or cork-tree, is a genus of deciduous, dioecious trees in the family Rutaceae, native to east and northeast Asia. It has leathery, pinnate leaves and yellow, clumped flowers. The name refers to the thick and corky bark of some species in the genus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Phellodendron_amurense0.jpg/330px-Phellodendron_amurense0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phellodendron","wikidata":"Q1539986"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Kanzou2012.jpg/500px-Kanzou2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Kanzou2012.jpg/1280px-Kanzou2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Kanzou2012.jpg/500px-Kanzou2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plant as used in Chinese herbology. Note the pictured is a photo of Licorice Root/ GanCao, not Phellodendron. (crude medicine)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKanzou2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Phellodendron_amurense_%2812%29.JPG/120px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2812%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Phellodendron_amurense_%2812%29.JPG/250px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2812%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Phellodendron_amurense_%2812%29.JPG/120px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2812%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhellodendron_amurense_(12).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Phellodendron_amurense_%2815%29.JPG/120px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2815%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Phellodendron_amurense_%2815%29.JPG/250px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2815%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Phellodendron_amurense_%2815%29.JPG/120px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2815%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhellodendron_amurense_(15).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Phellodendron_amurense_%2818%29.JPG/120px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2818%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Phellodendron_amurense_%2818%29.JPG/250px-Phellodendron_amurense_%2818%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2